Idea:
*banes can be #invoked to cause fear/confusion in all monsters in
sight.  (Come to think of it, fear and confusion might make good
wizard spells). Probably not demonband or dragonbane.

Were the powers of artifacts mostly set before weapon skills?  I think
weapon skills tend to increase the power of the mainstream weapon
types and decrease the power of the fringe ones, especially those
with highly specific use like Trollsbane.  I think the damage of most
banes should be increased to x3 at least, since most people using
them will be doing so at a -4/-2 or after burning a skill slot.

> Grayswandir: 1.5x damage instead of double

Bringing down the top doesn't seem right for some reason.
I think grayswandir could use a slight and subtle nerfing, but
that's a different thread...

> Trollsbane: kills trolls instantly (or trolls hit/killed by it don't
> regen?)

I like no ressies like everyone else. I think if it kills them they should
leave no corpse, either, with some satisfactory "the troll disappears
into noxious fumes" type message.

> Dragonsbane: kills dragons instantly (or dragons always leave scales?)

Both of these seem yucky. I think it might simply be really good at
killing them.  Perhaps make it a silver spear.  Perhaps have it grant
resistances to the common "bad" dragon types: fire, cold, shock,
and poison.

> Werebane: werefoo cannot summon help when wielded

Immunity to lycanthropy?   Perhaps it should also force them
back into human form when it hits them.

> Ogresmasher: kills ogres instantly

Probably too strong, but on the other hand, sure why not.


> Demonbane: does 2X damage against riders, as well (or more??)

2x vs. riders, 3x versus other &s?

> Tsurugi: always insta-kill engulfers

Including air elementals on their plane?

> Grimtooth (I forget this even exists sometimes): always poisoned

(Not sure what poisoning does to monsters...)

> Orcrist: 3X damage to orcs instead

Seems a good candidate for invoking for fear, although I'm not
sure orcs are ever a problem by the time most people get their
first artifact.

Perhaps give it bonuses in the hands of an orc.

